<Layout title="Privacy Policy · Cookie Dough Digital" description="How Cookie Dough Digital handles the details you share through our website, our chatbot Chip, and our lead forms.">
<section class="head on-marsh"><div class="container"><p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p><h1>Privacy Policy</h1><p class="lede">Effective date: November 19, 2026</p></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="container prose">
<h2>Who we are</h2>
<p>Cookie Dough Digital is a digital agency based in Bluffton, South Carolina. This page explains what personal information we collect through our website, our chatbot Chip, and our lead forms, why we collect it, and how you can reach us about it.</p>
<h2>What we collect</h2>
<h3>Our chatbot, Chip</h3>
<p>We load the chat tool only after you click the chat button. If you never open the chat, the chat tool does not create a contact.</p>
<p>When you click the chat button, the chat tool loads and may create a contact record before you type a message or agree to share your details. That record can include an anonymous visitor ID, your timezone, an approximate location (city, region, and country) based on your IP address, your browser type, and the welcome message.</p>
<p>If you ask us to set up a free call, request a Site Health Check through the chat, or otherwise leave your details, we collect:</p>
<ul>
<li>Your name (required)</li>
<li>Your email address (required)</li>
<li>Your phone number (optional)</li>
<li>Your business name and website address (optional; "no site yet" is fine)</li>
<li>Your business type or industry</li>
<li>What you need help with</li>
<li>Your town (Lowcountry or remote)</li>
<li>A preferred day and time window for a call. This is only a preference. It is not a booked appointment.</li>
<li>Where you found us</li>
<li>Your consent, and the time you gave it</li>
</ul>
<p>We will not save those lead details without your yes on a consent line, which also links to this page.</p>
<p>We do not ask for passwords, logins, payment details, or other sensitive information through the chatbot.</p>
<p>The chat conversation is stored by PayMeGPT, the company that runs the chat tool.</p>
<h3>Our contact form</h3>
<p>If you use the contact form on our website, we collect the information you enter and send it to PayMeGPT and a Google Sheet so we can follow up.</p>
<h3>Free Site Health Check</h3>
<p>A dedicated Health Check form is not live yet. Until it is, a Health Check request through the chatbot uses the same questions listed above, and a website address is required.</p>
<p>When a Health Check form launches, we expect it to ask for your name, work email, website address, business name, business type, city and ZIP, your role, whether you own the business, an authorization, and optionally a phone number and a note. We will update this page if those fields change. We also plan to keep a shared log of every Health Check request, including requests we decline.</p>
<p>If you use a personal webmail address, such as Gmail, Yahoo, Outlook, Hotmail, AOL, or iCloud, the request is reviewed with you before any free scan runs.</p>
<h2>Why we collect it</h2>
<p>We collect this information to:</p>
<ul>
<li>Respond to your request</li>
<li>Request a free call and agree on a time. This is not a booked appointment, and we do not use a public calendar to set the time</li>
<li>See whether we are a good fit, including a check against work we do not take on (commercial construction and home builders)</li>
<li>Run the free Site Health Check on the website you submit, once that process launches, including email verification when needed</li>
<li>Keep a record of requests so we can follow up</li>
<li>Understand where you found us, and which of our chat entry points you used, when we can tell</li>
</ul>
<p>We do not use your information to send marketing emails or to show you ads.</p>
<p>Until an automated email sender is set up, the chatbot's only acknowledgement is the message you see in the chat. A person at Cookie Dough Digital then follows up by hand.</p>
<h2>Who processes it</h2>
<p>These companies process information so we can handle your request:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>PayMeGPT</strong>, which runs the chatbot, contact records, the lead pipeline, and forms. PayMeGPT stores conversation data in the United States.</li>
<li><strong>Google</strong>, through a Google Sheet in our Google account that logs leads from the chatbot, the contact form, and, when it launches, the Health Check form</li>
<li><strong>The AI model provider</strong> configured for Chip. Your chat messages are sent to that provider so Chip can reply. The provider depends on the model we choose, and it can change if we change the model.</li>
<li><strong>Stripe</strong>, which the chat tool loads. Stripe may collect device signals and set a cookie used for fraud prevention.</li>
<li><strong>IP geolocation services</strong> used by PayMeGPT (ipapi.co and ip-api.com), which turn your IP address into an approximate city, region, and country</li>
</ul>
<p>We do not sell your personal information. We do not share it except with the processors above who help us handle your request.</p>
<p>We do not use Google Calendar to book calls. If we later send mail through a business email service, we will update this page before that starts.</p>
<h2>How long we keep it</h2>
<p>PayMeGPT keeps chat conversations for about two years, or until a deletion request, under PayMeGPT's policy.</p>
<p>We keep information in our Google Sheet and our own records only as long as we need it to respond to you and run our business, then we delete it. We may keep information longer if the law requires it.</p>
<h2>Your choices</h2>
<p>You can ask to see, correct, or delete your information by emailing or calling us at the contact details below. We'll respond within 30 days.</p>
<h2>Cookies and analytics</h2>
<p>Our website itself does not set cookies and does not use analytics. It does load Google Fonts, which means Google may receive your IP address.</p>
<p>When you open the chatbot, additional tools run:</p>
<ul>
<li>PayMeGPT uses local storage, session storage, and a service worker to run the chat and recognize a returning visitor</li>
<li>Stripe may set a third-party cookie (cookie name "m") that lasts about 13 months, and may collect device signals</li>
<li>The chat tool may also load fonts and icons from Google and from Cloudflare</li>
<li>In some browsers, the chat tool may use cookies if other storage is blocked</li>
</ul>
<p>We do not install a separate analytics service on our site. PayMeGPT records a view event when the chat tool loads. We do not claim this site is cookie-free once the chatbot is in use.</p>
<h2>Children</h2>
<p>This site is not directed to children under 15, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from children. PayMeGPT, the tool that runs the chat, is not intended for children under 16.</p>
<h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
<p>If we change this policy, we will update this page and the date at the top.</p>
<h2>Contact</h2>
<p>Cookie Dough Digital<br />Bluffton, South Carolina<br /><a href="mailto:cookiedoughdigital@gmail.com">cookiedoughdigital@gmail.com</a><br /><a href="tel:+18436033134">843-603-3134</a></p>
</div></section>
</Layout>
